# Short Coding Bank (with solutions)

## A) Core JS (Functions / Arrays / Strings)

### 1) Even/Odd
**Q:** Write `isEven(n)` returns true if even.  
**A:**
```js
function isEven(n) {
  return n % 2 === 0;
}
```

### 2) Reverse string
```js
function reverseString(s) {
  return s.split("").reverse().join("");
}
```

### 3) Count vowels
```js
function countVowels(s) {
  const m = s.match(/[aeiou]/gi);
  return m ? m.length : 0;
}
```

### 4) Sum array
```js
function sumArray(arr) {
  return arr.reduce((sum, x) => sum + x, 0);
}
```

### 5) Remove duplicates
```js
function unique(arr) {
  return [...new Set(arr)];
}
```

## B) DOM (common slide-style)

### 6) Button changes text
**HTML**
```html
<p id="msg">Hello</p>
<button id="btn">Change</button>
```
**JS**
```js
document.getElementById("btn").addEventListener("click", () => {
  document.getElementById("msg").textContent = "Changed!";
});
```

### 7) Add item to list from input
```js
document.querySelector("#add").addEventListener("click", () => {
  const text = document.querySelector("#item").value.trim();
  if (!text) return;

  const li = document.createElement("li");
  li.textContent = text;
  document.querySelector("#list").appendChild(li);

  document.querySelector("#item").value = "";
});
```

### 8) Simple form validation (email contains @)
```js
document.querySelector("#f").addEventListener("submit", (e) => {
  const email = document.querySelector("#email").value;
  if (!email.includes("@")) {
    e.preventDefault();
    document.querySelector("#err").textContent = "Invalid email";
  }
});
```

## C) OOP

### 9) Class with method
```js
class Student {
  constructor(name, id) {
    this.name = name;
    this.id = id;
  }
  info() {
    return `${this.name} (${this.id})`;
  }
}
```

### 10) Constructor function + prototype method
```js
function Rectangle(w, h) {
  this.w = w;
  this.h = h;
}
Rectangle.prototype.area = function() {
  return this.w * this.h;
};
```
